IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wpa-types`
IMPORT `wpa-deductions`
IMPORT `wpa-payment`
IMPORT `wpa-enforcement`

-- Wages Protection Act 1983 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this payment of wages: were the deductions lawful; were the wages
--    paid in a lawful manner; did the employer contravene the Act; and what
--    may the worker, or a Labour Inspector, recover from the employer under
--    s 11 in an action brought on the given day?"
--
-- One answer through Goals 1-3 (wpa-deductions.l4, wpa-payment.l4,
-- wpa-enforcement.l4). Premiums, spending and penalties (Goal 4) answer
-- their own questions in wpa-enforcement.l4.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Wage protection position` HAS
    `total deducted`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `lawful deductions`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `unlawful deductions`                               IS A NUMBER
    `the wages were paid in a lawful manner`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer contravened ss 4, 5, 5A or 7`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `recoverable for deductions (s 11(1)(a))`           IS A NUMBER
    `recoverable for payment otherwise than in money (s 11(1)(b))` IS A NUMBER
    `recoverable from the employer under s 11`          IS A NUMBER
    `wages neither paid nor deducted`                   IS A NUMBER

-- s 11(1)(b) "an amount equal to any wages required by section 7 to be paid
-- to that worker in money, if that employer paid those wages to that worker
-- otherwise than in money" — the amount paid in the unlawful manner, if the
-- action is in time (s 11(2)).
@ref s 11(1)(b), (2)
GIVEN c IS A `Wage payment case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount recoverable under s 11(1)(b) in` c MEANS
    IF      NOT `the wages were paid in a lawful manner` (c's `payment`)
        AND `an action under s 11 is in time, cause arose` (c's `payment`'s `paid on`) `, brought` (c's `action brought on`)
    THEN c's `payment`'s `amount paid`
    ELSE 0

@ref ss 4, 5, 5A, 6, 7-10, 11, 15, 16
@export default The wage protection position for one payment of wages under the Wages Protection Act 1983 (NZ): how much was deducted, how much of it lawfully (s 4: only with written consent or request for a lawful purpose, after consultation under a general deductions clause, not unreasonable, ss 5, 5A; or recovering an overpayment, up to the amount overpaid, s 6; or under another Act, collective agreement or order, ss 15, 16); whether the wages were paid in a lawful manner (ss 7-10); whether the employer contravened the Act; and what the worker or a Labour Inspector may recover from the employer under s 11 in an action brought on the given day. Deductions before 1 April 2016 are outside the Act as it now stands. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Wage payment case`  @desc The wages payable, how they were paid (manner, amount, date, consent, absence, ss 15-17 authority), the day an action is brought, and each deduction (amount, date, basis, lawful purpose, consultation, reasonableness, withdrawal)
GIVETH A `Wage protection position`
`the wage protection position for` c MEANS
    `Wage protection position` WITH
        `total deducted`                                IS total
        `lawful deductions`                             IS lawful
        `unlawful deductions`                           IS total MINUS lawful
        `the wages were paid in a lawful manner`        IS manner
        `the employer contravened ss 4, 5, 5A or 7`     IS (total MINUS lawful) GREATER THAN 0 OR NOT manner
        `recoverable for deductions (s 11(1)(a))`       IS fromDeductions
        `recoverable for payment otherwise than in money (s 11(1)(b))` IS fromManner
        `recoverable from the employer under s 11`      IS fromDeductions PLUS fromManner
        `wages neither paid nor deducted`               IS max 0 (c's `wages payable` MINUS c's `payment`'s `amount paid` MINUS total)
    WHERE
        total          MEANS sum (map (GIVEN d YIELD d's `amount`) (c's `deductions`))
        lawful         MEANS sum (map (GIVEN d YIELD `the lawful part of the deduction` d) (c's `deductions`))
        manner         MEANS `the wages were paid in a lawful manner` (c's `payment`)
        fromDeductions MEANS sum (map (GIVEN d YIELD `the amount recoverable under s 11(1)(a) for` d `, action brought` (c's `action brought on`)) (c's `deductions`))
        fromManner     MEANS `the amount recoverable under s 11(1)(b) in` c
